\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Low-dimensional consumer-resource dynamics accurately predict combinatorial synthetic gut assembly with complexity-invariant fidelity.} (A) Out-of-sample testing fit on 73 strictly held-out test communities from Venturelli et al.~\cite  {venturelli2018deciphering} across all dynamic timepoints ($t \in [12, 24, 36, 48, 60]$\,h; $K=7$ latent resources, $S=12$ species; $R^2 = 0.771$, Pearson $r = 0.880$, $N = 4,380$), with points colored by sampling timepoint. Dashed diagonal line indicates perfect parity ($y = x$). (B) Trajectory prediction accuracy (Pearson $r$) as a function of initial community Shannon diversity ($H$), demonstrating an absence of complexity-dependent performance decay (Pearson $r = -0.097,\ p = 0.414$; Spearman $\rho = -0.076,\ p = 0.521$). Dashed line and shaded band indicate linear regression fit with 95\% confidence interval; points are colored by species richness ($S$). (C) Invariance to compositional distance: trajectory prediction accuracy plotted against mean Bray-Curtis distance to the training distribution ($r = +0.005,\ p = 0.969$; Spearman $\rho = -0.007,\ p = 0.951$), confirming robust generalization to compositionally novel consortia.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ophelia_assembly}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Low-dimensional consumer-resource dynamics accurately predict combinatorial synthetic gut assembly with complexity-invariant fidelity.} (A) Out-of-sample testing fit on 73 strictly held-out test communities from Venturelli et al.~\cite {venturelli2018deciphering} across all dynamic timepoints ($t \in [12, 24, 36, 48, 60]$\,h; $K=7$ latent resources, $S=12$ species; $R^2 = 0.771$, Pearson $r = 0.880$, $N = 4,380$), with points colored by sampling timepoint. Dashed diagonal line indicates perfect parity ($y = x$). (B) Trajectory prediction accuracy (Pearson $r$) as a function of initial community Shannon diversity ($H$), demonstrating an absence of complexity-dependent performance decay (Pearson $r = -0.097,\ p = 0.414$; Spearman $\rho = -0.076,\ p = 0.521$). Dashed line and shaded band indicate linear regression fit with 95\% confidence interval; points are colored by species richness ($S$). (C) Invariance to compositional distance: trajectory prediction accuracy plotted against mean Bray-Curtis distance to the training distribution ($r = +0.005,\ p = 0.969$; Spearman $\rho = -0.007,\ p = 0.951$), confirming robust generalization to compositionally novel consortia}{figure.1}{}}
