\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Model-inferred adhesion partitioning validates disruptive selection driven by serial transfer mechanics.} (A) Log-scale distribution of the adhesion partitioning ratio ($\log _{10}(k_{\text  {attach}}/k_{\text  {shed}})$) across all 50 strains in Mucin Agar, showing a statistically significant bimodal distribution (Gaussian Mixture Model $\Delta \text  {BIC} = -10.9$). Mode 1 ($\text  {ratio} \approx 0.22$, 35\% of strains) corresponds to Planktonic Opportunists; Mode 2 ($\text  {ratio} \approx 1.82$, 65\% of strains) corresponds to Biofilm Specialists. (B) In Plain Agar, the distribution shifts sharply to a planktonic-dominated regime (71.4\% in Mode 1, 28.6\% in Mode 2). (C) Cross-condition comparison illustrating how mucin recruits the biofilm colonizer guild. (D) Schematic of the physical transfer mechanics: tweezers transfer 20\% of beads while supernatant is diluted 30-fold (3.5\% transfer), creating an evolutionary fitness valley for intermediate generalists.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pollard_bimodal}{{3}{5}{\textbf {Model-inferred adhesion partitioning validates disruptive selection driven by serial transfer mechanics.} (A) Log-scale distribution of the adhesion partitioning ratio ($\log _{10}(k_{\text {attach}}/k_{\text {shed}})$) across all 50 strains in Mucin Agar, showing a statistically significant bimodal distribution (Gaussian Mixture Model $\Delta \text {BIC} = -10.9$). Mode 1 ($\text {ratio} \approx 0.22$, 35\% of strains) corresponds to Planktonic Opportunists; Mode 2 ($\text {ratio} \approx 1.82$, 65\% of strains) corresponds to Biofilm Specialists. (B) In Plain Agar, the distribution shifts sharply to a planktonic-dominated regime (71.4\% in Mode 1, 28.6\% in Mode 2). (C) Cross-condition comparison illustrating how mucin recruits the biofilm colonizer guild. (D) Schematic of the physical transfer mechanics: tweezers transfer 20\% of beads while supernatant is diluted 30-fold (3.5\% transfer), creating an evolutionary fitness valley for intermediate generalists}{figure.3}{}}
